%%%
export const meta = { title: "Nota Mega-Test" };

const Box = blockComponent((children) => @div[class: "box"]{@children});
const Aside = blockComponent((children) => @aside{@children});
const Colorized = inlineComponent((children) => {
  let [color, setColor] = useState("red");
  return @span[onClick: () => setColor("green")][style: {color}]{@children};
});

const name = "Will";
const url = "/home";
const disabled = true;
const rest = { id: "demo" };
const items = ["x", "y", "z"];
const i = 1;
const ui = { Card: Box };
const comps = { card: Box };
const k = "card";
const getTag = () => "section";
%%%

# Nota Mega-Test

A *terse* tour of _every_ Nota feature, written by @name,
spanning a soft line break.

@Aside{A block component nesting @b{markup} and an empty @span{}.}

## Elements & props

A @a[href:"/x"][title:"home"]{static link}, a @a[href:url]{dynamic link}, and an
@input[type:"text", disabled, ...rest] self-closing field. A @figure[cap:@em{a caption}]{body}
carries a markup-valued prop; balanced braces stay literal: @p{a set {1, 2, 3}}.

Dynamic tags: @(Box){direct}, @(ui.Card){member}, @(getTag()){call}, @(comps[k])[n:1]{computed}.
Also a @{bare @b{fragment}} and an expression @(1 + 2).

## Control flow

@if (items.length > 2) {Many}
else if (items.length > 0) {Some}
else {None} items.

@ul{
  @for (x of items) {@li{@x}}
  @for ([key, val] of [["a", 1], ["b", 2]]) {@li{@key = @val}}
  @for ({ id } of [{ id: 1 }, { id: 2 }]) {@if (id) {@li{row @id}}}
}

## Markup sugar

Emphasis nests: *bold with _italic_ within*; intra-word stays literal in my_var_name and 2*3*4.

###### A level-6 heading

- bullet one
- bullet two
  - nested bullet
- bullet three with a
  wrapped continuation line
+ ordered one
+ ordered two
1. explicit one
2. explicit two

## Raw spans

Inline `f(x)` code, math $x^2$ with interpolation $a_@i$ and $b_@(i + 1)$, and display math:

$$\sum_@(items.length) x_i$$

Escapes render literally: \* \_ \# \$ \@ \{ \} and a backslash \\.

```python
def f(x):
    return x
```

@pre|{
@foo{x} is raw; |@Colorized{this is a child} and |@name interpolates.
}|

## Colon & block sugar

@summary: A one-line colon-sugar element.

@section:
  | class: "tip"
  A block-sugar body with a prop line
  and a soft-broken continuation.

## Nested statements

@aside{
  An intro sibling.
  % const count = items.length
  @p{Then @count items, wrapped in an IIFE.}
}

## Doc-state sugar

An anchor <sec-flow> and a reference &sec-flow resolve; a footnote[^n1] and a
repeat[^n1] share a number, plus a second[^n2]. Literal Vec<T> and R&D stay text.

[^n1]: The first footnote body, with @em{markup}.
[^n2]: The second footnote body.
